# Buildroot users table — additional accounts created at rootfs
# assembly time. See
#   https://buildroot.org/downloads/manual/manual.html#makeuser-syntax
# Format: username uid group gid password home shell groups comment
#
# `wash` is the unprivileged user wash-router drops to via su(1)
# from S99wash-router. Empty password ("=") because login via getty
# isn't a normal user-facing path here; the shell tab is for the
# debugger. Sudo policy in /etc/sudoers.d/wash-nopasswd grants
# passwordless sudo to all commands (wash-priv detects this at
# startup and skips the FE password modal — see priv's
# detectPasswordlessSudo + skipPassword).
wash -1 wash -1 = /home/wash /bin/sh - "wash desktop user"
